==Overview==
===x980-32CQ===

'''<font color="blue">OEM's from WMC - created to our requirements</font>'''

The x980-32CQ is the first variant of the x980 switch family. 

*It has 32 100G QSFP28 fixed slot ports and no XEM bays or PHYs.
*The 100G ports will also support 40G. 31 of the QSFP28 network ports will support 1-to-4 octopus breakout cables, which will allow 25G and 10G links.
*The x980-32CQ has five fan trays.
*It will support VCS-4 stacking.

[[File:X980-32CQ front imag.png]]

[[File:X980-32CQ rear image.png]]

The x980-32CQ switchchip is the Falcon 98CX8522 model, which has 3.2Tbps of bandwidth and 128 x 28G I/O [2].<section begin="overview" /><section end="overview" />

===x980-32DQ===

'''<font color="blue">OEM's from WMC - based on another customers requirements as it is already MassPro for them</font>'''

The x980-32DQ is the second x980 variant.

*This is the highest speed x980, with 32 400G QSFP-DD fixed slot ports and no XEM bays or PHYs.
*The 400G ports will also support 100G. 31 of the QSFP-DD network ports will support 1-to-4 octopus breakout cables, which will allow 100G and 25G links.
*The x980-32DQ has six fan trays.
*It will support VCS-4 stacking.

[[File:X980-32DQ front image.png|725x725px]]

[[File:X980-32DQ rear image.png|662x662px]]

The x980-32DQ switchchip is the Falcon 98CX8580 model, which has 12.8Tbps of bandwidth and 256 x 56G I/O [2].

====<font color="red">x980-32DQ Known Issues </font>====


{{StorytHead|X980|586}}

*2.5M DAC cables will only link up with other Marvell device at 400G.
*x980-32DQ to x980-32DQ should work

[[File:32DQ Limitation 01.png|725x725px]]

===x980-16CDQ===

'''<font color="blue">Designed by ATI-SJ</font>'''

*x980-16CDQ (w/ 24x100G + 8x400G port capacity)
*For data center applications
*Marvell’s Prestera 98CX85xx (Falcon) series Switch chipset
*Eight zQSFP+ fixed ports that support 100G / 200G Optical modules / DAC cables
*Eight QSFP-DD fixed ports that support 400G / 200G / 100G Optical modules / DAC cables
*Two XEM slots that support XEM3-8CQ, XEM3-2DQ, XEM3-12XTm, XEM3-12YS pluggable

[[File:X980-32CDQ-updated-front.png|758x758px]]

[[File:X980-32CDQ-rear-updated.png|754x754px]]

The serdes lanes on the x980-16CDQ are divided differently to accommodate the different port speeds.

[[File:X980-32CDQ serdes.png|550x550px]]

